    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddStruct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddSemigroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deprecated</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"no replacement\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">since</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"2026-09-27\"</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulStruct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semigroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">deprecated</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deprecated</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"no replacement\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">since</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"2026-09-27\"</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_thm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semigroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulStruct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulStruct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Removing the <code>set_option</code> gives linter warning</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>MulStruct</code> has been deprecated: no replacement</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Came up in review of <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37298\">#37298</a></p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span></p>",
        "id": 627452051,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1790605013
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm... This was implemented in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40503\">#40503</a>. <br>\nSpeculation: my guess is that it has to do with the application time of the <code>to_additive</code> attribute (which is late, so that we can add <code>simp</code> attributes correctly). Maybe the linters are called before then, so they don't have access yet to the fact that <code>to_additive</code> will soon add the deprecation attribute?<br>\nIf so, I'm not sure if there is an easy fix...</p>",
        "id": 627499771,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1790615076
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"479299\">@Jovan Gerbscheid</span></p>",
        "id": 627499798,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1790615086
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It looks like Lean uses <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Elab.Term.withDeprecationContextFromAttrs#doc\">docs#Lean.Elab.Term.withDeprecationContextFromAttrs</a> to help decide whether deprecations should be warned about. This function does a hard-coded check to see if any of the attributes are the <code>deprecated</code> attribute.</p>\n<p>So, with the current design, we can't fix this problem. What we could do is to change the syntax so that instead of <code>@[to_additive (attr := deprecated ...)]</code>, we write <code>@[deprecated ..., to_additive]</code> (this was actually my original approach in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40503\">#40503</a>), but that is probably less intuitive.</p>",
        "id": 627505233,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1790616403
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One issue with that is that one might want to \"additivise\" the deprecation message (as in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37298\">#37298</a>)</p>",
        "id": 627525580,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1790621211
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that <code>to_additive</code> and <code>deprecated</code> have the same (late) application time, so this should not be an issue:</p>\n<p>if you write <code>@[to_additive, deprecated ...]</code>, then <code>to_additive</code> will not be aware of the deprecation, while in <code>@[deprecated ..., to_additive]</code>, it would be.</p>",
        "id": 627527117,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1790621627
    }
]